2. **`value = value.strip()`**: Removes leading and trailing whitespace from the dish name. This ensures consistency in comparing names.
3. **`if re.search(r'\([^)]*\)', value):`**: Checks if there are any parenthetical descriptions within the dish name (e.g., "(READY)").
4. **`value = re.sub(r'\([^)]*\)', '', value).strip()`**: If parentheses are found, this line removes the entire content within them along with the parentheses themselves. The `.strip()` is applied again to remove any potential extra whitespace introduced by the removal.
5. **`return value`**: Returns the cleaned dish name without parenthetical descriptions.



